<title>UK: Bradford wool market eases, further falls likely.</title>
<headline>Bradford wool market eases, further falls likely.</headline>
<dateline>BRADFORD 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Topmakers quotations slipped as much as five pence per kilo with further falls thought to be likely.</p>
<p>Sterling's strength was said to be hampering the UK wool market as this makes overseas wool cheaper, with higher UK interest rates adding fuel to this particular fire.</p>
<p>However, at present deliveries are often said to be going out well and machinery was keeping active, brokers said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8074</p>
